{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the goat of the sin offering.</b> According to the plain sense, it is the one about which it says 'take a goat of the goats' etc., for here and there atonement is stated for it." "<b>The goat of the sin offering.</b> Rashi explained: the goat of the new month offerings and three sin-offering goats were offered on that day — a goat of the goats, Nahshon's goat, and the goat of the new month — and of all of them only this one was burned, meaning of those three goats only this one of the new month was burned, and it was burned with the priest's knowledge. And Rashi further explained: one may say that because of impurity that touched it, it was burned. And if you ask: was it not anyway liable to be burned, for it is impossible that there were not those impure through corpse-contact from the day they were born, and they touched this goat, and they had not yet been purified by the sprinkling of the third and seventh day — for they did not yet have ashes of a cow until the next day, as we maintain: on the first of Nisan the Tabernacle was erected, on the second the cow was burned — one may answer: to purify it from the anointing oil and from the blood that is on the altar, like Aaron and his sons. As we say in tractate Yoma: you might say the waters entered under the blood."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:14.444581338Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}